  "version": 2,
  "name": "Boss OC-2 Octaver (35000)",
  "description": "Boss OC-2 Octaver, catalogue 35000. Single +9 V supply with a +4.9 V reference. Divider: the factory's IC6 BA634 'reference / flip-flop / buffer' function is fitted as its documented block (discrete comparators + one CD4013B half used as the squarer latch), followed by the two uPD4013C halves that make f/2 and f/4 - the same three-flip-flop chain the Busser redraw and the Sabro build draw, but with the stock 4013 part in every position (no 4027: the factory parts list has none). Shaper and divider wiring from the Busser 1999 redraw; values cross-checked against the 1982 service notes and champ.pdf.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "B. Busser, 'BOSS OCTAVE OC2 MODIFIED', 1999-08-23",
      "note": "Cadence redraw, vector-clean: shaper, comparator and divider wiring (a modified unit: TL074/TL072, J110, MC14013/MC14027)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Boss OC-2 Service Notes 1982-05-10 sheet BB-2 1",
      "note": "factory parts list and values: IC1-5 TL022CP, IC6 BA634, IC7 uPD4013C, 2SK30ATM-Y, D10/D11 1S188FM Ge"
    },
    {
      "title": "champ.pdf pp.1,5 (OC-2 compilation)",
      "note": "factory parts list re-confirmed; p5 states the architecture: IC5b mixes the input with the 1/2 square wave, IC5a mixes the OCT1 signal with the 1/4 square wave, and '4013 ou 4027' for the divider"
    },
    {
      "title": "Harald Sabro, Modified OC-2 Octaver",
      "note": "second redraw plus measured pin voltages on a working unit"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stellan Lehrberg OC-2 redraw",
      "note": "third document, used for the LOG/band-pass values"
    }
  ],
  "io": {
    "input": "in",
    "output": "out"
  },
  "oversampling": 2,
